// REP-19: a file's top-level statements are its program. §3.2 says so — "top-level
// statements are wrapped in a generated entry function" — and until ADR-067 they
// were analyzed and then dropped, so this file printed nothing.
//
// There is no `fn main` here at all, which is how §3.2, §3.3 and §4.2 are written.
out(1)
let x = 2
out(x)
var y = x
y = y + 1
out(y)
